From: =?UTF-8?q?Ga=C3=ABl=20Duval?= <gael@murena.io>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 13:24:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] feat(word): Word-like style gallery options and live
 style preview

- asc_SetStyleGalleryOptions({wordLike, previewText, width, height}):
  list the styles as Word does (Quick Styles only; Heading 3-9 once the
  level above is used; Caption, TOC Heading and semi-hidden styles once
  used; styles without priority last), draw a sample text such as
  "AaBbCcDd" instead of the style name, set the preview size even when
  the painter already exists. asc_UpdateStyleGallery() regenerates.
- asc_StartStylePreview(name) / asc_EndStylePreview(): apply a style to
  the selection inside a group action with interface events off, and
  revert it without an undo point (gallery hover); nothing is sent to
  co-authors meanwhile; spell checking is turned back on afterwards.
- Fixes: the gallery sorted styles of equal priority on CStyleImage.Name,
  which does not exist (the field is "name"), so they kept a random
  order; now case-insensitive with numeric order (Heading 1..9).
  Character style previews applied the style to the paragraph and showed
  plain text; they now format the run.
Default behaviour is unchanged without the options.

[upstreamable]

Assisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5
